{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Zebulun shall dwell by the shore of the seas.</b> The order of the tribes here follows the correct order according to their lineage: the first six are the sons of Leah, then he arranged as one Dan and Gad and Asher and Naphtali, who are the sons of the handmaids, and after that he arranged Joseph and Benjamin, who are the sons of Rachel. And it would have been fitting to precede Issachar before Zebulun, because Issachar was born first, but he preceded Zebulun because the Torah of Issachar is sustained through him (Zebulun); and so Moses our master, peace be upon him, also gave him precedence (Deuteronomy 33:18): ״שמח זבולון בצאתך ויששכר באהליך״." "And the sense of <b>shall dwell by the shore of the seas</b> (is): by the shore of the seas shall his land be, and there he shall be found constantly, for he is engaged in commerce and provides sustenance for the tribe of Issachar, who are engaged in Torah; and consequently the merit of Zebulun is great, for he is the cause of the Torah of Issachar. And this is what is written (Ecclesiastes 7:12): ״כי בצל החכמה בצל הכסף״ — the word 'shadow' (בצל) is from the language of nobility (אצילות), and its meaning is: the nobility of wisdom is sustained through the nobility of money. And for this reason Scripture gave Zebulun precedence over Issachar." "<b>And you should</b> discern that Zebulun alludes to the central line that connects above and below, and this is the meaning of 'the shore of the seas' (לחוף ימים), in the manner of (Genesis 1:10) ״ולמקוה המים קרא ימים״, and it is in the manner of (Psalms 19:6) ״והוא כחתן יוצא מחופתו״, and this is clear."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:21:33.514973455Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}